WEBVTT

NOTE
Fictional demonstration data - no live searches or MSX writes.
Search/AI backend responses and waits are simulated/compressed. No narration.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.858
Prepare a Connect from evidence, not a tab tour.
Fictional data only. Search/AI responses and waits are simulated/compressed.

2
00:00:06.858 --> 00:00:22.813
Confirm the date window; reuse completed coverage.
Only missing closed dates are searched. Existing saved evidence is retained.

3
00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:29.346
Queued is not Running: two date ranges run at most.
A queued range waits for a slot; it has not begun searching.

4
00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:38.336
Sources returned does not mean full date coverage.
Results must be checked and saved; an incomplete source keeps its dates open.

5
00:00:38.336 --> 00:00:47.890
Search ended incomplete: saved evidence stays available.
Retry incomplete sources searches only the unfinished source—not the whole window.

6
00:00:47.890 --> 00:01:00.048
The email-only Retry moves back into the queue.
The superseded warning disappears; successful searches and saved evidence are retained.

7
00:01:00.048 --> 00:01:09.403
Review verified history without verifying it again.
An earlier saved contribution only needs its goal placement confirmed.

8
00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:15.652
Early-careers delivery: verify a completed outcome.
Confirm what you delivered and who benefited—not attendance alone.

9
00:01:15.652 --> 00:01:21.914
Community or ERG contribution: verify the actual impact.
The adopted accessibility checklist is a concrete completed contribution.

10
00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:28.121
Learning or credential completed: check completion proof.
Completed learning belongs under the skilling goal, not delivery credit.

11
00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:34.371
Compliance completed: use the completion record.
A certificate supports a completed compliance contribution.

12
00:01:34.371 --> 00:01:39.938
Compliance awaiting confirmation is a different category.
This source is only a reminder: Exclude instead of claiming completion.

13
00:01:39.938 --> 00:01:46.153
Coaching or mentoring delivered: distinguish direction.
Delivered coaching is attributable; mentoring received stays supporting context.

14
00:01:46.153 --> 00:01:52.370
Reusable asset or innovation created: verify the reuse.
The sample-data tool is an outcome, not a proposed activity.

15
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:58.602
External speaking or advocacy: verify the delivered event.
Retain the specific talk and the reusable outcome.

16
00:01:58.602 --> 00:02:04.835
When classification is unclear, change the details.
Choose the contribution type, goal and section before verifying.

17
00:02:04.835 --> 00:02:16.803
Customer delivery: inspect the source, then confirm context.
Link the real customer, opportunity and matching milestone before Verify and use.

18
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:24.447
Keep useful customer/account work without an MSX link.
General context is a valid explicit placement; it is not a goal achievement.

19
00:02:24.447 --> 00:02:33.014
Historical milestone context is reference-only.
It does not join a deal team or confer ownership, current delivery or revenue credit.

20
00:02:33.014 --> 00:02:41.297
CSU handover — no new revenue requirement confirmed.
Record the recipient and context; do not claim the receiving team’s later delivery.

21
00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:49.616
Another SE/team handover keeps the original contribution.
Record the recipient and context; do not claim the receiving team’s later delivery.

22
00:02:49.616 --> 00:02:57.930
An opportunity-only link is also supported.
Do not invent a milestone when the source supports only the opportunity.

23
00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:07.878
If the customer is unclear, verification waits for your choice.
Search the loaded accounts, select Contoso, then save an account-only contribution.

24
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:12.389
A saved Goal 2 attach claim can need a separate decision.
Without structured attach proof, move the advice to its appropriate goal.

25
00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:17.893
Supporting context is not an approved achievement.
Mentoring received stays here; it does not become mentoring delivered.

26
00:03:17.893 --> 00:03:22.709
Customer-only and historical work remains retained.
Account-held evidence and handovers are separate from current MSX delivery.

27
00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:32.774
Confirmed goal-linked evidence sits under its goal.
General context stays separate; verification and goal placement are different decisions.

28
00:03:32.774 --> 00:03:37.593
General context is an explicit saved choice, not a missing goal.
Use verified-history filters to see the records kept outside goal achievements.

29
00:03:37.593 --> 00:03:45.026
Now generate the Connect from the reviewed evidence.
This offline AI response is simulated; the output uses the actual current renderer.

30
00:03:45.026 --> 00:03:51.072
A populated draft appears, with saved length guidance.
Looking for missed contributions runs automatically below that advisory.

31
00:03:51.072 --> 00:04:03.762
Review missed verified contributions before accepting them.
Select the useful item and draft additions; the generated answer is not silently changed.

32
00:04:03.762 --> 00:04:14.114
Accept the useful addition by editing the answer yourself.
Save answer creates a separate working copy; the generated original remains protected.

33
00:04:14.114 --> 00:04:24.973
Change the depth of one answer without regenerating all four.
Question 2 becomes Concise. Other answers—including the accepted addition—stay unchanged.

34
00:04:24.973 --> 00:04:37.116
Read the final populated draft, then copy the answer or all four.
The missed contribution is included. Check the character counts before using your wording.

35
00:04:37.116 --> 00:04:42.380
End to end: retrieve, recover, verify, place, generate, review and save.
Fictional demonstration only. No live searches, live data or MSX writes.
